// EXPECT: [E122]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 12,
// A return is COVARIANT: a pointer whose return type is refined promises its callers that range,
// and the call's result is typed by the pointer. `zero()` returns 0 as `*func() Pos`, so
// `100 / g()` was "proven" nonzero. The parent compiled it: a division by zero natively,
// --interpret 99 ("division by zero (proven nonzero)"). I.187
type Pos = i32 >= 1 and <= 9
func zero() i32 {
    return 0
}
func main() i32 {
    var g *func() Pos = zero
    return 100 / g()
}
